From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 13:07:56 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Split chunk generation into a shaping half and a finishing
 half

shapeChunk does noise, biome lookup, surface replacement, caves and ravines.
It writes only into a ChunkSnapshot nobody can see yet and reads nothing from
the World but its seed and the generate-x flags, so it is a pure function of
(seed, x, z).

finishChunk does structure starts, builds the Chunk and lights it. Structure
starts stay here because they mutate a map and a persistent NBT record that
/locate, ender eyes and mob-spawn checks read from the server thread. They
still run after caves and ravines and before the Chunk is built, so blocks
land in the same order.

createShapingCopy rebuilds the generator from the seed for use on a worker,
because rand, the noise buffers and biomesForGeneration are per-instance
scratch and cannot be entered twice at once. The copy carries its own
WorldChunkManager for the same reason and does not touch the world.

getOrCreateChunk calls both halves back to back, so nothing changes yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

