+    // Athena start - the half of generation that never looks at the World.
+    //
+    // Noise, biome lookup, surface replacement, caves and ravines all write into a ChunkSnapshot
+    // that nothing else can see yet, and read nothing from the world beyond its seed and the
+    // generate-x config flags. That makes this a pure function of (seed, x, z) and safe to run on a
+    // worker - on a copy of this generator, since the scratch fields it uses are per-instance.
+    //
+    // Structure starts deliberately stay behind in finishChunk: they mutate a map and a persistent
